{% comment %}
  Looks one option value up in the map built by `swatch-fallback-map`.
  Outputs the colour, or nothing when the name has no entry — callers treat
  an empty result as "no swatch available" and keep the text control rather
  than drawing a blank chip.

  Accepts:
  - map: {String} output of `swatch-fallback-map`
  - name: {String} the option value's name

  Usage:
  {%- capture fallback_color -%}
    {%- render 'swatch-fallback-color', map: map, name: value.name -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign needle = name | strip | downcase
  assign entries = map | split: '||'
  for entry in entries
    assign parts = entry | split: '~'
    if parts[0] == needle
      echo parts[1]
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
